  "widgets": ["TextWidget", "SelectWidget", "RadioWidget"],
  "description": "NASA - PI and AOR (Nasa_PIandAORSupplementalDataSheet) asks NASA applicants for the names of the authorized organization representative (AOR) and the principal investigator (PI), the AOR's NSPIRES username, and whether the PI takes part as an employee of the U.S. Government, with the agency and amount requested if so, or of a foreign organization.",
  "notes": [
    "The DAT's conditional rules are not in the form yet (#13368): Federal Agency is enabled and required, and the dollar amount enabled, only if the PI is a U.S. Government employee; International Participation is disabled and set to No if so.",
    "The dollar amount is a string of up to 12 digits with optional cents, as in the API's budget forms. The XML mapping writes it with two decimal places."
  ],
  "risks": [
    "The DAT and FID still show the OMB expiration as 09/30/2026. OMB renewed 2700-0092 on 11/03/2026 through 11/30/2029 (reginfo.gov), so the form uses the renewed date.",
    "The XSD's header names OMB numbers 2700-0085 and 2700-0087, which were discontinued in 2013. The form uses 2700-0092, as the DAT and FID do."
  ],
